prompt:
{
  "public_instructions": "You translate natural-language access-control requirements into Cedar policies using the supplied schema. Cedar denies by default. An applicable forbid overrides every permit. Guard optional attributes with has before reading them. Preserve the schema's entity, set, and attribute types. Use only the supplied task information. Do not use tools, files, search, additional model calls, or external feedback. Produce a single final answer as a JSON object with exactly one field, policy, whose value is the complete Cedar policy text. Do not include explanations or Markdown fences.
",
  "harness": {
    "instruction_blocks": [
      "Translate the access-control requirements into a complete Cedar policy set. Identify each action, eligible principal, resource type, required condition, prohibition, and exception. Use only entity types, attributes, actions, and representations supported by the schema. Implement the stated permissions and restrictions together.",
      "Before answering, check the policy mentally for both unauthorized permissions and missing required permissions. Keep distinct action rules separate when their conditions differ. Apply exceptions only to the restriction they qualify. Return one final policy set."
    ],
    "input_order": [
      "requirements",
      "schema"
    ],
    "checklist": [
      "Every required action is covered.",
      "Role, ownership, membership, and context conditions follow the requirements.",
      "Prohibitions and exceptions compose correctly.",
      "Optional attribute reads are guarded and Cedar syntax is valid."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": "The system manages the approval and release of bank wire transfers.
The people involved are originators, verifiers, treasury officers, and compliance reviewers. One person may hold both the originator and verifier roles at the same time.
The resources are wire transfers and accounts. Every wire transfer records who initiated it, who verified it, who screened it, its account, its amount, its fee, its amount tier, its beneficiary, its currency code, whether it is high risk, and its status. Every account records its holder and its allowed beneficiaries.
Each request carries the current time, the daily cutoff, whether it came from the secure network, whether multi-factor authentication was used, and whether an emergency has been declared.
In this workflow a wire is first approved and then released, and the release step can see the wire's status and who verified it as recorded by the earlier steps.
A person may approve a wire only when their authority tier is at least as high as the wire's amount tier, and a person whose authority tier is below the wire's amount tier may not approve it.
A wire may be approved only when its amount plus fee crosses the set threshold, and a request to approve one whose amount plus fee stays at or below that threshold is refused.
A wire may be released only after it has been verified, and a request to release one that has not been verified is refused.
A wire may be released only when its beneficiary is on the account's screened allowlist, and a request to release one to a beneficiary not on that allowlist is refused.
A wire may be released only when its amount crosses the set money threshold, and a request to release one whose amount stays at or below that threshold is refused.
Neither a verifier nor a treasury officer may approve a wire whose amount tier exceeds their authority tier.
A run through the workflow by a verifier whose authority tier is at least the wire's amount tier, where the amount plus fee crosses the threshold so the verifier approves it, and where a treasury officer then releases the verified wire to an allowlisted beneficiary for an amount above the money threshold, tripping no prohibition above, must be able to succeed.",
  "schema": "entity Person {
    isOriginator: Bool,
    isVerifier: Bool,
    isTreasuryOfficer: Bool,
    isComplianceReviewer: Bool,
    authorityTier: Long,
};

entity Account {
    holder: Person,
    allowedBeneficiaries: Set<String>,
};

entity WireTransfer {
    initiatedBy: Person,
    verifiedBy?: Person,
    screenedBy: Person,
    account: Account,
    amount: decimal,
    fee: decimal,
    amountTier: Long,
    beneficiary: String,
    currencyCode: String,
    isHighRisk: Bool,
    status: String,
    approvalThreshold: Long,
    moneyThreshold: Long,
    amountPlusFeeExceedsApprovalThreshold: Bool,
    amountExceedsMoneyThreshold: Bool,
};

entity Beneficiary;

entity WireStatus enum ["Approved", "Released"];

action approveWire appliesTo {
    principal: [Person],
    resource: [WireTransfer],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        dailyCutoff: datetime,
        cameFromSecureNetwork: Bool,
        mfaUsed: Bool,
        emergencyDeclared: Bool,
        approvalThreshold: decimal,
    },
};

action releaseWire appliesTo {
    principal: [Person],
    resource: [WireTransfer],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        dailyCutoff: datetime,
        cameFromSecureNetwork: Bool,
        mfaUsed: Bool,
        emergencyDeclared: Bool,
        releaseMoneyThreshold: decimal,
    },
};
"
}
